# Runtime Dev Dev Notes — Hardware-Aware Init Retry + Context Creation Retry

**Date:** 2026-05-04  
**Branches covered:**

```text
hardware-aware-degraded-init-retry-v1
context-creation-retry-v1
```

**Purpose:** preserve behavior, caveats, hidden contracts, and future-assistant guidance for the last two Runtime Dev branches. This document emphasizes behavior that is not obvious from reading individual code files.

---

## High-Level Branch Relationship

These two branches are related but intentionally separate.

```text
hardware-aware-degraded-init-retry-v1
  -> handles model/init retry, validated init-time configOverride, hardware-aware profile planning, worker config snapshots.

context-creation-retry-v1
  -> handles per-session worker-local createContext retry after the model is already loaded.
```

Do not blur these layers:

```text
init retry != context creation retry
configOverride != retry strategy
hardware probe metadata != createContext options
model load config != context allocation config
prompt retry != context retry
```

The hardware-aware branch may select safer starting config/profiles during initialization. The context-retry branch retries `model.createContext(...)` when session context creation fails.

