## Branch 2 — Context Creation Retry v1

### Core Behavior

This branch adds retry around worker-local session context creation:

```text
getSession(sessionId)
  if session exists: return it
  maybe evict oldest
  create context through retry profiles
  create LlamaChatSession
  store wrapper only after success
```

The feature is scoped to:

```js
model.createContext(...)
```

It is not:

```text
model-load retry
prompt retry
generation retry
native operation cancellation
tool calling
drain shutdown
```

### Files Added / Modified

```text
config.mjs
contextRetryProfiles.mjs
inference.mjs
llama_worker/llama.mjs
tests/smokeTestContextCreationRetry.mjs
```

### Required Config Placement

`creationRetry` belongs under:

```js
context: {
    creationRetry: { ... }
}
```

It must not be under:

```js
modelLoad: {
    creationRetry: { ... } // wrong
}
```

This placement error happened once during the branch. Always verify it explicitly.

### Important Non-Obvious Behavior

#### 1. `creationRetry` is not part of `configOverride` in v1

Do not add `context.creationRetry` to the `configOverride` surface in this branch.

Reason: `inference.mjs` currently decides whether context retry needs passive probe data from the base config. That remains safe only because `configOverride` cannot change `creationRetry`.

Future warning:

```text
If configOverride.context.creationRetry is ever allowed, createInitPlan() must decide probing from the effective config candidate, not base config.
```

#### 2. Context retry profiles are worker-local but generated by helper

`contextRetryProfiles.mjs` builds profiles for the worker to consume:

```text
base-context
batch-safe-context
bounded-context-safe
conservative-context
```

`maxAttempts` slices the deduplicated profile ladder. Default is:

```text
maxAttempts: 4
```

Profile dedupe is based on the createContext-option signature, not deep semantic equivalence.

#### 3. `creationRetry` must not leak into `model.createContext(...)`

The helper deletes `creationRetry` from generated profile contexts.

The worker also uses:

```js
toContextCreateOptions(profile.context)
```

as an allowlist before calling:

```js
model.createContext(...)
```

This double layer matters. Keep both.

#### 4. Hardware probe metadata must not leak into `createContext`

`inference.mjs` may attach:

```js
hardwareProbe
```

to the outbound worker `configSnapshot`.

That metadata is for helper profile planning only. It must not reach `model.createContext(...)`.

The worker’s `toContextCreateOptions()` prevents this.

#### 5. Context retry can trigger passive probe even without hardware-aware init strategy

Context retry adds a second reason to probe:

```text
1. hardware-aware init strategy needs probe
2. context.creationRetry.enabled !== false &&
   context.creationRetry.allowHardwareDerivedBounds === true
```

This means default init may now perform passive CPU/RAM probing even when `strategy` is still `same-config-cold-worker`.

Users can disable this through static config:

```js
context: {
    creationRetry: {
        enabled: false
        // or
        allowHardwareDerivedBounds: false
    }
}
```

#### 6. `lastSuccessfulProbe` is separate from effective config

`inference.mjs` stores probe metadata separately:

```text
lastSuccessfulEffectiveConfig
lastSuccessfulProbe
```

Do not mutate the effective config to stash probe data. Reset fixed re-init should carry `lastSuccessfulProbe` into the worker config snapshot separately.

#### 7. Memory-pressure cap wins

Accepted policy:

```text
Retry context bounds are derived from hardware/config fallback, then capped by the base context bounds so retry never increases context memory pressure relative to the failed base attempt.
```

If base `contextSize` is fixed or bounded, retry fallback must not exceed that base attempt.

Examples:

```text
baseContextSize: 2048
fallback: { min: 1024, max: 4096 }
result: { min: 1024, max: 2048 }

baseContextSize: 512
fallback: { min: 1024, max: 4096 }
result: { min: 512, max: 512 }

baseContextSize: { min: 512, max: 1024 }
fallback: { min: 1024, max: 4096 }
result: { min: 512, max: 1024 }

baseContextSize: "auto"
result: normal configured/hardware bounded fallback
```

The counterintuitive part: configured `minContextSize` is not an absolute lower bound if the failed base attempt is smaller. The base cap wins.

Reason: retry should recover from allocation failure, not request a larger allocation than the failed attempt.

#### 8. Fallback batch must not increase base batch

If base `batchSize` is already smaller than `fallbackBatchSize`, keep the smaller base value.

This mirrors the memory-pressure policy for context size.

#### 9. Context creation failures are request-scoped, not init-scoped

Context creation happens during `getSession()` for a prompt/session after model init. If all profiles fail, the worker should return a prompt/request error such as:

```text
Context creation failed after N attempt(s).
Session: <sessionId>.
Attempted profiles: ...
Last error: ...
```

Do not route these as model init failures.

#### 10. Partial cleanup failure aborts retry

Worker v2 behavior:

```js
disposePartialSessionArtifacts(...)
```

attempts cleanup and then throws the first cleanup error if cleanup fails.

This is intentional. Do not keep retrying after a partial context/session cleanup failure.

Reason: continuing after failed disposal risks native resource leakage or inconsistent worker state.

#### 11. Obsolete/canceled state is checked around await boundaries

The worker checks obsolete/canceled state:

```text
before createContext attempt
after createContext/session creation failure
after successful context/session creation before storing wrapper
```

This handles cases where a prompt is canceled/reset while an awaited operation is in progress.

Caveat: if native `createContext()` blocks the worker message loop, cancel/reset may not be observed until `createContext()` returns. Preemptive native cancellation is out of scope for v1.

#### 12. Session reuse bypasses retry

If a session already exists:

```js
if (sessions.has(sessionId)) return sessions.get(sessionId);
```

then no context retry happens. Retry is only for creating a new session context.

#### 13. Eviction still happens before new context creation

If `sessions.maxCount` is reached, the oldest session is disposed before creating a new one.

This behavior was preserved. No rollback layer was added if new context creation fails after eviction.

