## Diagnostic / Testing Caveats From This Branch

### Fixture path-resolution trap

A temporary isolation test that copied the runtime tree into `.tmp-reset-isolation-*` changed the worker-relative model path resolution.

Production worker model path logic:

```js
const modelPath = path.resolve(
    __dirname,
    `${config.modelLoad.baseModel}`
);
```

When the worker file is copied to a different directory depth, the same relative `../../../base/...` no longer points to the same place.

Do not diagnose production model-load behavior from a copied fixture unless the fixture also patches `baseModel` to an absolute path or preserves directory depth exactly.

### Native hard-exit / heat/resource noise

During testing, a Windows native child-process exit occurred once around `model reset idle` with code:

```text
3221226505
```

Narrow reset isolation modes later passed, and the lifecycle regression child/full orchestrator passed after rerun. Treat similar single hard exits as serious signals, but isolate before assuming a deterministic code regression.

Good isolation sequence:

```bash
SMOKE_MODE=lifecycle-regression node ./tests/smokeTestLifecycleRegression.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestLifecycleRegression.mjs
```

If reset-specific:

```text
reset-no-session
reset-after-one-session
reset-after-two-sessions
reset-after-session-reset
```

Avoid copied-runtime fixture modes unless the model path issue is solved.

### Heat clamp delays are not failures

Heat clamp/sleep messages appeared during local tests. These are runtime/environment throttling behavior and not test failures.

