## Workflow Lessons / Guardrails

### Do not trust generated artifacts until reopened and guarded

During context retry work, several bad artifacts/canvases were produced before the workflow was tightened:

```text
bad patch
bad zip
wrong config placement
invalid full-module canvas
stale worker file without v2 cleanup fix
missing smoke test in branch
```

Correct flow:

```text
source material check
plan alignment check
stage one file
copy-completeness check
recognized-patch review
cross-file propagation review
fix concrete issues
re-review
only then rebuild artifacts
run artifact guard
then run local tests
then verify GitHub
```

### Use the toolbox where it fits

Useful tools:

```text
impact_map.py
  -> structural propagation/import surface review

artifact_guard.py
  -> required files, forbidden files, placement anchors, syntax checks

line_profile_compare_tool.py
  -> fallback copy/completeness check when hashing or visual review is unreliable
```

The line-profile tool is not proof of identical content. Same-length substitutions can still pass. It is a fallback structural completeness signal.

### GitHub raw/file fetch may be visually misleading

A raw/view fetch appeared line-collapsed during branch verification, but content anchors were correct. Do not assume formatting is broken unless local `git diff` or the GitHub UI confirms it.

